Thanks everyone who responded to my posting...  Sorry, but since you're all
across the pond I'm not allowed to mail you.

One point that came up and which may be a spoiler is as follows...

If the machine slows down, you are either in a level with a Throneroom,
Morgue, barracks or zoo (David's very own treasure park), you could also
be on one of the pre-prepared engame levels (don't worry, you should be
powerful enough by the time you get down there).

Just a minor spoiler to take the surprise out of finding a monster room.

Speaking of which, I've been watching for some time now someone playing NetHack
on a Sun (latest version from what I see)... he hasn't come across any beehives
yet.  We grepd the source and couldn't find 'bee'!  Are the hives still
implemented, is he unlucky, or hasn't he got far enough?  I hat the places
personally since the bees either gang up and kill me or the last one (Murphy's
Law and not the source code dictates this) always gives me an instant-death, no
chance to save yourself sting.  Either that or I kill myself eating the jelly!

Anyway, are they implemented, and where might I find a beehive (what level
about)?

Tim Brown.


